oys approximately 44K people. Revenue per employee of $284K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $250 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Community Health Systems, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $312M market cap on $12.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and -6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $208M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 98% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 43% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Community Health Systems' (NYSE:CYH) Problems Go Beyond Weak Profit","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-cyh/community-health-systems/news/community-health-systems-